// GPU settings preset: low-tablet
//
// The smallest preset: a texture edge of 256 voxels and 1 GB of texture
// memory. Almost every volume exceeds that edge, so a viewport reduces its
// texture, and the reduction is easy to see. Compare it with `gpu/medium`,
// which reduces far less, and with `gpu/high-texture-4096`, which reduces
// nothing.
//
// A preset applies only with final downsampling on, and a preset in this
// customization turns final downsampling on, also in a locked-down config.
// `?customization=` needs `customizationUrlPrefixes`, and config/default.js has
// none: there, set the preset through `customizationService` in the config.
// Nothing probes the device: a preset is a set of values, so a real device may
// hold more or less than the preset states.
//
// Load it with `?customization=gpu/low-tablet`.
{
  "bootstrap": {
    "cornerstone.gpuSettingsPreset": "low-tablet"
  }
}
